<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hautes-Pyrénées</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hautes-Pyrénées is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> on the Spanish border, in the Occitanie region, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarbes">Tarbes</a> as its prefecture. It covers the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adour">Adour</a> valley, and roughly corresponds to the old County of Bigorre. It includes the pilgrimage town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lourdes">Lourdes</a> and the Pic du Midi observatory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hautes-pyrenees.jpg" alt="Hautes-Pyrénées" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saüquère · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pr%C3%A9fecture_des_Hautes-Pyr%C3%A9n%C3%A9es.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
